Output:
## Implementation
- camel/memories/agent_memories.py
  - Classes: ChatHistoryMemory, VectorDBMemory, LongtermAgentMemory
  - Note: LongtermAgentMemory augments ChatHistoryMemory with VectorDBMemory for persistent longterm memory.

- camel/toolkits/human_toolkit.py
  - Class: HumanToolkit
  - Functions: ask_human_via_console (two-way human interaction), send_message_to_user (one-way user notification)
  - Provides tools for human interaction usable by agents.

## Examples (MOST IMPORTANT)
- examples/memories/agent_memory_example.py
  - Shows usage of ChatAgent with ChatHistoryMemory and memory saving/loading.
  - Demonstrates memory persistence and interaction with multiple agents.

- examples/toolkits/human_toolkit.py
  - Shows usage of ChatAgent with HumanToolkit tools.
  - Demonstrates asking human questions and sending messages to user via agent tools.

## Tests
- test/memories/test_agent_memories.py
  - Tests for LongtermAgentMemory and ChatHistoryMemory functionalities.

# Summary
To create an agent with longterm memory and human interaction tools, use:
- LongtermAgentMemory from camel/memories/agent_memories.py for memory
- HumanToolkit from camel/toolkits/human_toolkit.py for human interaction tools
- ChatAgent from camel/agents/chat_agent.py (imported in examples)

The examples in examples/memories/agent_memory_example.py and examples/toolkits/human_toolkit.py provide usage patterns for memory and human tools respectively.

You can combine these patterns to create your script at task-script/single_agent/9_longterm_memory_single_agent.py.
